  "word_times_path": "/Users/diplomat/ytvideos/channels/paper_detour/videos/045_edmund_fitzgerald_last_voyage/Edit/Timeline/word_times_en_v01.json",
  "audio_path": "/Users/diplomat/ytvideos/channels/paper_detour/videos/045_edmund_fitzgerald_last_voyage/Source/Audio/mix_en_v01.wav",
  "audio_sha256": "46e4a989af29d5807e999acd711d68b0ea08b874076e46e76d85aaafab7b67da",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "scene_id": "S01",
      "composition_source": "S01",
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 153,
      "duration_frames": 153,
      "start_seconds": 0.0,
      "end_seconds": 5.1,
      "spoken_text": "In November 1975, a massive cargo ship called the Edmund Fitzgerald ",
      "first_word": "In",
      "last_word": "Fitzgerald"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S02",
      "composition_source": "S02",
      "start_frame": 153,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 300,
      "duration_frames": 147,
      "start_seconds": 5.1,
      "end_seconds": 10.0,
      "spoken_text": "was crossing Lake Superior. On board were 29 people and more than 26,000",
      "first_word": "was",
      "last_word": "26,000"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S03",
      "composition_source": "S03",
      "start_frame": 300,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 441,
      "duration_frames": 141,
      "start_seconds": 10.0,
      "end_seconds": 14.7,
      "spoken_text": "tons of iron ore.\n\nThe next day, the ship disappeared ",
      "first_word": "tons",
      "last_word": "disappeared"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S04",
      "composition_source": "S04",
      "start_frame": 441,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 590,
      "duration_frames": 149,
      "start_seconds": 14.7,
      "end_seconds": 19.666667,
      "spoken_text": "during a storm. No one heard a distress call. And just minutes before it is believed ",
      "first_word": "during",
      "last_word": "believed"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S05",
      "composition_source": "S05",
      "start_frame": 590,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 734,
      "duration_frames": 144,
      "start_seconds": 19.666667,
      "end_seconds": 24.466667,
      "spoken_text": "to have gone down, the crew was still answering radio calls from the bridge.\n\n",
      "first_word": "to",
      "last_word": "bridge"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S06",
      "composition_source": "S06",
      "start_frame": 734,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 876,
      "duration_frames": 142,
      "start_seconds": 24.466667,
      "end_seconds": 29.2,
      "spoken_text": "What happened between that final conversation and the ship's disappearance remains unknown to ",
      "first_word": "What",
      "last_word": "to"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S07",
      "composition_source": "S07",
      "start_frame": 876,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 1028,
      "duration_frames": 152,
      "start_seconds": 29.2,
      "end_seconds": 34.266667,
      "spoken_text": "this day.\n\nThe Edmund Fitzgerald left the port of Superior on November 9. ",
      "first_word": "this",
      "last_word": "9"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S08",
      "composition_source": "S08",
      "start_frame": 1028,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 1176,
      "duration_frames": 148,
      "start_seconds": 34.266667,
      "end_seconds": 39.2,
      "spoken_text": "Its destination was the Detroit area, where it was supposed to deliver its cargo after crossing Lake ",
      "first_word": "Its",
      "last_word": "Lake"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S09",
      "composition_source": "S09",
      "start_frame": 1176,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 1325,
      "duration_frames": 149,
      "start_seconds": 39.2,
      "end_seconds": 44.166667,
      "spoken_text": "Superior. For a ship more than 200 meters long, this was another routine ",
      "first_word": "Superior",
      "last_word": "routine"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S10",
      "composition_source": "S10",
      "start_frame": 1325,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 1474,
      "duration_frames": 149,
      "start_seconds": 44.166667,
      "end_seconds": 49.133333,
      "spoken_text": "voyage across the Great Lakes.\n\nAnother freighter, the Arthur M. Anderson, was heading ",
      "first_word": "voyage",
      "last_word": "heading"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S11",
      "composition_source": "S11",
      "start_frame": 1474,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 1619,
      "duration_frames": 145,
      "start_seconds": 49.133333,
      "end_seconds": 53.966667,
      "spoken_text": "in the same direction. The two ships stayed in radio contact. As the weather ",
      "first_word": "in",
      "last_word": "weather"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S12",
      "composition_source": "S12",
      "start_frame": 1619,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 1767,
      "duration_frames": 148,
      "start_seconds": 53.966667,
      "end_seconds": 58.9,
      "spoken_text": "began to deteriorate, both changed course toward the Canadian shore, hoping it would offer some ",
      "first_word": "began",
      "last_word": "some"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S13",
      "composition_source": "S13",
      "start_frame": 1767,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 1920,
      "duration_frames": 153,
      "start_seconds": 58.9,
      "end_seconds": 64.0,
      "spoken_text": "protection from the waves.\n\nBut on November 10, the storm grew stronger. ",
      "first_word": "protection",
      "last_word": "stronger"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S14",
      "composition_source": "S14",
      "start_frame": 1920,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 2066,
      "duration_frames": 146,
      "start_seconds": 64.0,
      "end_seconds": 68.866667,
      "spoken_text": "The wind shifted direction, and enormous waves built up on the eastern side of the ",
      "first_word": "The",
      "last_word": "the"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S15",
      "composition_source": "S15",
      "start_frame": 2066,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 2210,
      "duration_frames": 144,
      "start_seconds": 68.866667,
      "end_seconds": 73.666667,
      "spoken_text": "lake. Snow reduced visibility. Both ships were now trying to reach the more ",
      "first_word": "lake",
      "last_word": "more"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S16",
      "composition_source": "S16",
      "start_frame": 2210,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 2357,
      "duration_frames": 147,
      "start_seconds": 73.666667,
      "end_seconds": 78.566667,
      "spoken_text": "sheltered waters of Whitefish Bay.\n\nThat afternoon, the Fitzgerald reported ",
      "first_word": "sheltered",
      "last_word": "reported"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S17",
      "composition_source": "S17",
      "start_frame": 2357,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 2506,
      "duration_frames": 149,
      "start_seconds": 78.566667,
      "end_seconds": 83.533333,
      "spoken_text": "damage. Part of its deck railing had been damaged, there were problems with its ventilation equipment, ",
      "first_word": "damage",
      "last_word": "equipment"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S18",
      "composition_source": "S18",
      "start_frame": 2506,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 2649,
      "duration_frames": 143,
      "start_seconds": 83.533333,
      "end_seconds": 88.3,
      "spoken_text": "and the ship had developed a list. Its pumps were running.\n\nLater, its ",
      "first_word": "and",
      "last_word": "its"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S19",
      "composition_source": "S19",
      "start_frame": 2649,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 2799,
      "duration_frames": 150,
      "start_seconds": 88.3,
      "end_seconds": 93.3,
      "spoken_text": "radars failed. The Fitzgerald was sailing ahead, while the Anderson followed behind, ",
      "first_word": "radars",
      "last_word": "behind"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S20",
      "composition_source": "S20",
      "start_frame": 2799,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 2955,
      "duration_frames": 156,
      "start_seconds": 93.3,
      "end_seconds": 98.5,
      "spoken_text": "helping over the radio by reporting the ship's position relative to the shore and other vessels.\n\n",
      "first_word": "helping",
      "last_word": "vessels"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S21",
      "composition_source": "S21",
      "start_frame": 2955,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 3104,
      "duration_frames": 149,
      "start_seconds": 98.5,
      "end_seconds": 103.466667,
      "spoken_text": "That evening, the Anderson contacted the crew again and asked how they were managing their ",
      "first_word": "That",
      "last_word": "their"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S22",
      "composition_source": "S22",
      "start_frame": 3104,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 3252,
      "duration_frames": 148,
      "start_seconds": 103.466667,
      "end_seconds": 108.4,
      "spoken_text": "problems.\n\nThe reply from the Fitzgerald was simple: “We are holding our own.”\n\n",
      "first_word": "problems",
      "last_word": "own"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S23",
      "composition_source": "S23",
      "start_frame": 3252,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 3404,
      "duration_frames": 152,
      "start_seconds": 108.4,
      "end_seconds": 113.466667,
      "spoken_text": "That was the last known radio contact.\n\nSoon afterward, the Fitzgerald's radar ",
      "first_word": "That",
      "last_word": "radar"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S24",
      "composition_source": "S24",
      "start_frame": 3404,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 3545,
      "duration_frames": 141,
      "start_seconds": 113.466667,
      "end_seconds": 118.166667,
      "spoken_text": "echo disappeared from the screen. When visibility improved, its lights were gone ",
      "first_word": "echo",
      "last_word": "gone"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S25",
      "composition_source": "S25",
      "start_frame": 3545,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 3692,
      "duration_frames": 147,
      "start_seconds": 118.166667,
      "end_seconds": 123.066667,
      "spoken_text": "too. Repeated radio calls went unanswered.\n\nThe Anderson reported the ",
      "first_word": "too",
      "last_word": "the"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S26",
      "composition_source": "S26",
      "start_frame": 3692,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 3839,
      "duration_frames": 147,
      "start_seconds": 123.066667,
      "end_seconds": 127.966667,
      "spoken_text": "disappearance to the Coast Guard. Then, after reaching sheltered waters, the freighter ",
      "first_word": "disappearance",
      "last_word": "freighter"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S27",
      "composition_source": "S27",
      "start_frame": 3839,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 3983,
      "duration_frames": 144,
      "start_seconds": 127.966667,
      "end_seconds": 132.766667,
      "spoken_text": "turned around and headed back into the storm to help with the search.\n\nLifeboats and other ",
      "first_word": "turned",
      "last_word": "other"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S28",
      "composition_source": "S28",
      "start_frame": 3983,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 4131,
      "duration_frames": 148,
      "start_seconds": 132.766667,
      "end_seconds": 137.7,
      "spoken_text": "debris were found. There were no survivors. All 29 people aboard the ",
      "first_word": "debris",
      "last_word": "the"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S29",
      "composition_source": "S29",
      "start_frame": 4131,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 4279,
      "duration_frames": 148,
      "start_seconds": 137.7,
      "end_seconds": 142.633333,
      "spoken_text": "Edmund Fitzgerald had died.\n\nLater, search equipment located the wreck at a ",
      "first_word": "Edmund",
      "last_word": "a"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S30",
      "composition_source": "S30",
      "start_frame": 4279,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 4428,
      "duration_frames": 149,
      "start_seconds": 142.633333,
      "end_seconds": 147.6,
      "spoken_text": "depth of about 160 meters. The ship lay in two main sections. ",
      "first_word": "depth",
      "last_word": "sections"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S31",
      "composition_source": "S31",
      "start_frame": 4428,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 4576,
      "duration_frames": 148,
      "start_seconds": 147.6,
      "end_seconds": 152.533333,
      "spoken_text": "The bow was upright, while the stern was upside down.\n\nBut even the discovery ",
      "first_word": "The",
      "last_word": "discovery"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S32",
      "composition_source": "S32",
      "start_frame": 4576,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 4728,
      "duration_frames": 152,
      "start_seconds": 152.533333,
      "end_seconds": 157.6,
      "spoken_text": "of the wreck did not provide a final answer to the central question: what exactly ",
      "first_word": "of",
      "last_word": "exactly"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S33",
      "composition_source": "S33",
      "start_frame": 4728,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 4874,
      "duration_frames": 146,
      "start_seconds": 157.6,
      "end_seconds": 162.466667,
      "spoken_text": "happened in those last few minutes?\n\nThe United States Coast Guard concluded that water ",
      "first_word": "happened",
      "last_word": "water"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S34",
      "composition_source": "S34",
      "start_frame": 4874,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 5024,
      "duration_frames": 150,
      "start_seconds": 162.466667,
      "end_seconds": 167.466667,
      "spoken_text": "had probably been entering the cargo hold gradually through hatch covers that were not sufficiently ",
      "first_word": "had",
      "last_word": "sufficiently"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S35",
      "composition_source": "S35",
      "start_frame": 5024,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 5168,
      "duration_frames": 144,
      "start_seconds": 167.466667,
      "end_seconds": 172.266667,
      "spoken_text": "watertight. As more water entered, the ship settled lower and lower in the ",
      "first_word": "watertight",
      "last_word": "the"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S36",
      "composition_source": "S36",
      "start_frame": 5168,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 5319,
      "duration_frames": 151,
      "start_seconds": 172.266667,
      "end_seconds": 177.3,
      "spoken_text": "lake.\n\nThe National Transportation Safety Board offered a different explanation for the final ",
      "first_word": "lake",
      "last_word": "final"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S37",
      "composition_source": "S37",
      "start_frame": 5319,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 5470,
      "duration_frames": 151,
      "start_seconds": 177.3,
      "end_seconds": 182.333333,
      "spoken_text": "stage of the disaster. According to its theory, water may also have been accumulating ",
      "first_word": "stage",
      "last_word": "accumulating"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S38",
      "composition_source": "S38",
      "start_frame": 5470,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 5620,
      "duration_frames": 150,
      "start_seconds": 182.333333,
      "end_seconds": 187.333333,
      "spoken_text": "inside the ship, but then one or more hatch covers gave way under the pressure of ",
      "first_word": "inside",
      "last_word": "of"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S39",
      "composition_source": "S39",
      "start_frame": 5620,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 5770,
      "duration_frames": 150,
      "start_seconds": 187.333333,
      "end_seconds": 192.333333,
      "spoken_text": "the water, causing the cargo hold to flood rapidly.\n\nThese were the conclusions of ",
      "first_word": "the",
      "last_word": "of"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S40",
      "composition_source": "S40",
      "start_frame": 5770,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 5918,
      "duration_frames": 148,
      "start_seconds": 192.333333,
      "end_seconds": 197.266667,
      "spoken_text": "investigations, not a record of the ship's final moments. No one from the ",
      "first_word": "investigations",
      "last_word": "the"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S41",
      "composition_source": "S41",
      "start_frame": 5918,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 6075,
      "duration_frames": 157,
      "start_seconds": 197.266667,
      "end_seconds": 202.5,
      "spoken_text": "Fitzgerald returned to explain what happened.\n\nWe know the route it took, its final radio ",
      "first_word": "Fitzgerald",
      "last_word": "radio"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S42",
      "composition_source": "S42",
      "start_frame": 6075,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 6228,
      "duration_frames": 153,
      "start_seconds": 202.5,
      "end_seconds": 207.6,
      "spoken_text": "messages, and where the wreck lies today. But between the words “We are holding our ",
      "first_word": "messages",
      "last_word": "our"
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "S43",
      "composition_source": "S43",
      "start_frame": 6228,
      "end_frame_exclusive": 6389,
      "duration_frames": 161,
      "start_seconds": 207.6,
      "end_seconds": 212.966667,
      "spoken_text": "own” and the loss of the ship, there is still a gap that has never been fully reconstructed.",
      "first_word": "own",
      "last_word": "reconstructed"
    }
  ],
